# The board runs under the Gunyah hypervisor, so systemd's virt detection
# (systemd-detect-virt -> vm-other) makes hostnamed report Chassis=vm even
# though there is no DMI and the hardware is an embedded SBC. GNOME reads that
# chassis type and hides the power-panel's automatic-suspend group and the
# power-button-behaviour row on anything it thinks is a VM, so both were
# missing from Settings on the QuecPi Alpha.
#
# CHASSIS is hostnamed's highest-priority source, so this overrides the
# detected value with no change to the hypervisor detection itself.
#
# embedded, not desktop: it is neither in the vm/tablet/handset exclusion
# list (so the suspend rows stay) nor in the tablet/watch/handset list that
# switches the delay dropdown to the short mobile times.
CHASSIS=embedded
